    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, sporting a robust 81.88 score against Xzavion Curry. With a favorable 5.68 xERA opposing him and a potent dynamic platoon advantage (+14%), **Gunnar Henderson** is our most reliable engine for counting stats. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Kyle Tucker** (75.28) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.84), both of whom benefit significantly from exploitable SP matchups. **Jackson Merrill** also projects exceptionally well at 71.56, bolstered by a +14% park factor that makes him a priority start despite a moderate challenge from Mason Adams.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who finished with a 47.59 efficiency score. While his 0.380 xwOBA remains high, the optimizer favored the higher cumulative floor provided by the middle-to-bottom of our active lineup; **Miguel Vargas** remains the first candidate for pinch-hit duties should any of the marginal starts\u2014specifically **Dominic Smith** (40.95) or **Wade Meckler** (47.47)\u2014show signs of stagnant production. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Jackson Merrill**, as their assumed spots are pending official confirmation.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the back end of the roster. **Dominic Smith** faces a tough L/L matchup against Shota Imanaga, and his low 40.95 score puts him on a short leash to ensure we maximize our daily game cap efficiency. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** was excluded today despite his speed upside because of a brutal draw against Zack Wheeler (3.24 xERA); his negative modifiers for SP skill and batting order position outweighed his stolen base potential in this specific simulation. We continue to hold **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, hoping for a return to reinforce the core as we approach the season\u2019s final stretch.",
